---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const schema = [
  {
    "@type": "AboutPage",
    "@id": "https://thisishowwesee.com/about#webpage",
    url: "https://thisishowwesee.com/about",
    name: "About Howie Seay",
    mainEntity: { "@id": "https://thisishowwesee.com/#howie" },
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="About Howie Seay — Product Leader & Board-Certified Cytometrist"
  description="Howie Seay: fifteen years of product development in scientific instruments, analysis software, and automated cell therapy manufacturing. Two granted patents."
  schema={schema}
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Howie <span class="accent">Seay</span></h1>
      <p>
        Good data is still harder to get than it should be. I build the instruments and software
        that close the gap between the question and an answer: flow cytometry,
        spectral analysis, and automated cell therapy
        manufacturing. Underneath all three it is the same job — work out what people actually
        need, make the case for building it, and see it through to something they can use.
        Consulting work runs through <a href="/">How We See LLC</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">01 / Focus</p>
      <h2>What I work on</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--text-dim); margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
        Three threads, one idea: measurement you can trust, at the scale medicine needs.
      </p>

      <div class="feature-grid">
        <article class="feature-card">
          <p class="feature-kicker">Cell therapy manufacturing</p>
          <h3>Making the automated line real</h3>
          <p>
            Product for the Cell Shuttle at Cellares: orchestration, scheduling, reagent and
            information management across four teams and 30+ engineers. That includes the
            traceability that lets the platform make real patient doses under FDA-regulated quality
            systems.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="feature-card">
          <p class="feature-kicker">Cytometry &amp; spectral</p>
          <h3>Fifteen years on the instruments</h3>
          <p>
            Conventional and full spectral, panel design, cell sorting, and the troubleshooting that
            keeps a core running. Named inventor on a granted method for modeling and minimizing
            spillover spreading, and board certified as a Specialist in Cytometry.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="feature-card">
          <p class="feature-kicker">Science into software</p>
          <h3>Requirements from the bench, not the boardroom</h3>
          <p>
            Gathered face to face with the scientists who use the thing, at the booth, on site, in the
            lab. Then come the business cases, pricing, and roadmaps that survive contact with
            reality.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">02 / Record</p>
          <h2>The long version</h2>
          <p>
            Fifteen years of it: fee-for-service cytometry and sorting cores at the University of
            Florida, panel design and spectral unmixing at BD and FlowJo, a genomics platform at
            Rosalind, and now automated cell therapy manufacturing at Cellares. Two granted patents,
            a stack of publications, and a peer review habit.
          </p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a href="/cv" class="button special">View CV</a>
            <a href="/pubs" class="button">Publications</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="split-media">
          <img src="/images/pic01.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">03 / Resources</p>
      <h2>Flow cytometry, mapped</h2>
      <p>
        A curated guide to the field: the communities worth joining, the books worth reading, the
        software worth learning, and the courses worth the time. Everything I wish someone had
        handed me on day one.
      </p>
      <a href="/flowsites" class="button">Browse the resources</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">04 / Elsewhere</p>
          <h2>Get SH*t Done</h2>
          <p>
            GS*D helps small businesses grow, with skill-building workshops for the DIY-inclined and
            full project management for anyone ready to hand it off. Consultation, education,
            facilitation. Run by Danielle Seay.
          </p>
          <a
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/danielle-seay-96628a172/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="button">Get serviced</a
          >
        </div>
        <div class="logo-panel">
          <img src="/images/pic11.jpg" alt="Get SH*t Done — consultation, education, facilitation" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div class="odds-viz" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 400 220" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
            <defs>
              <linearGradient id="g1" x1="0" x2="1">
                <stop offset="0" stop-color="#22d3ee" /><stop offset="1" stop-color="#8b5cf6" />
              </linearGradient>
              <linearGradient id="g2" x1="0" x2="1">
                <stop offset="0" stop-color="#8b5cf6" /><stop offset="1" stop-color="#ec4899" />
              </linearGradient>
            </defs>
            <g font-family="IBM Plex Mono, monospace" font-size="11" fill="#6b7889">
              <text x="0" y="26">ORDER UP</text>
              <text x="0" y="70">CALL TRUMP</text>
              <text x="0" y="114">GO ALONE</text>
              <text x="0" y="158">PASS</text>
              <text x="0" y="202" fill="#98a4b3">EXPECTED POINTS</text>
            </g>
            <g>
              <rect x="118" y="14" width="252" height="14" fill="rgba(242,245,247,.06)" rx="2" />
              <rect x="118" y="14" width="196" height="14" fill="url(#g1)" rx="2" />
              <rect x="118" y="58" width="252" height="14" fill="rgba(242,245,247,.06)" rx="2" />
              <rect x="118" y="58" width="151" height="14" fill="url(#g1)" rx="2" />
              <rect x="118" y="102" width="252" height="14" fill="rgba(242,245,247,.06)" rx="2" />
              <rect x="118" y="102" width="68" height="14" fill="url(#g2)" rx="2" />
              <rect x="118" y="146" width="252" height="14" fill="rgba(242,245,247,.06)" rx="2" />
              <rect x="118" y="146" width="106" height="14" fill="rgba(242,245,247,.18)" rx="2" />
            </g>
            <g font-family="IBM Plex Mono, monospace" font-size="10" fill="#98a4b3">
              <text x="330" y="202" text-anchor="end">+0.74</text>
            </g>
            <line x1="118" y1="188" x2="370" y2="188" stroke="rgba(242,245,247,.12)" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">05 / Projects</p>
          <h2>Things built to settle an argument</h2>
          <p>
            Side projects tend to start as a question nobody could answer at the table. The Euchre
            odds simulator runs Monte Carlo trials across your hand, seat, and the upcard to work out
            whether calling is the right move, then shows its reasoning.
          </p>
          <a href="/euchre" class="button">Run the numbers</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">06 / Contact</p>
      <h2>Let's talk</h2>
      <p>
        Flow cytometry, product work in life sciences, or something else entirely. Email reaches me
        directly; LinkedIn works too.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a href="mailto:howie@thisishowwesee.com" class="button special"
          >howie@thisishowwesee.com</a
        >
        <a
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/this-is-how-we-see/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="button">Connect on LinkedIn</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
